                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel%27s+theorem"} Gabriel's theorem
            (
            %a{:href => "#Gabriel72"}> Gabriel 72
            ) says that connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quivers"} quivers
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indecomposable+object"} indecomposable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+representations"} quiver representations
            over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed field
            are precisely the
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dynkin+quivers"} Dynkin quivers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/undirected+graph"} undirected graph
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dynkin+diagram"} Dynkin diagram
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} ADE series
          %p
            Moreover, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indecomposable+object"} indecomposable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+representations"} quiver representations
            in this case are in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/root+%28in+representation+theory%29"} roots
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/root+system"} root system
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dynkin+diagram"} Dynkin diagram
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            In the following we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
            for the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            (typically
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕂
                  %mo =
