          %p
          #IndecomposableRepsOfAn.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indecomposable+object"} indecomposable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+representations"} quiver representations
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_n
              are labeled by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b \in \mathbb{N}^2
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi b
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq a \leq b \leq n
              and are given as follows (see also
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#CarlssonDeSilva10"} Carlsson &amp; de Silva 2010
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "#Oudot15"} Oudot 15, p. 17
