          %p
          #RelationToPersistencyModules.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IndecomposableRepsOfAn"}
              is of key relevance in the discussion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistent+homology"} persistent homology
              (notably in
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+data+analysis"} topological data analysis
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+representation"} quiver representation
              is called a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zigzag+persistence"} zig-zag
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistence+module"} persistence module
              and the statement of Ex.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IndecomposableRepsOfAn"}
              is interpreted as saying that every persistence module is spanned by elements which
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %em appear
                  at some
                  %em resolution
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %li
                %p
                  %em persist
                  across a range
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo −
                          %mi a
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b - a
              %li
                %p
                  %em disappear
                  at some resolution
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiset"} multiset
              of these
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b)
              is then called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/barcode"} barcode
              or
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistence+diagram"} persistence diagram
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistence+module"} persistence module
            %p
              This relation between quiver representation theory and persistent homolology was originally highlighted by
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#CarlssonDeSilva10"} Carlsson &amp; de Silva 2010
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} ADE classification
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dynkin+quiver"}> Dynkin quiver
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/McKay+quiver"} McKay quiver
          %h2#references References
          %p The result is due to
          %ul
            %li#Gabriel72
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Gabriel"}> Peter Gabriel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Unzerlegbare Darstellungen. I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01298413"} doi:10.1007/BF01298413
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %em Quiver representations and Gabriel’s theorem
              (
              %a{:href => "https://www2.math.ethz.ch/education/bachelor/seminars/hs2009/clualg/Cluster-A5.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabriel%27s_theorem"} Gabriel’s theorem
          %p
            Re-proof of Gabriel’s theorem in the case of A-type quivers and relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistent+homology"} persistent homology
          %ul
            %li#CarlssonDeSilva10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gunnar+Carlsson"}> Gunnar Carlsson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vin+de+Silva"} Vin de Silva
              = succeed "," do
                %em Zigzag Persistence
              %strong 10
              (2010) 367–405
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.0197"} arXiv:0812.0197
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10208-010-9066-0"} doi:10.1007/s10208-010-9066-0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p reviewed in:
          %ul
            %li#Oudot15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Y.+Oudot"}> Steve Y. Oudot
